def LAD(*a): return list(a)
def RUB(a,b,c,d): return [(a,'Missing or unclear','Meets the stated check',b),(c,'Guessing','Evidence kept',d),('Records','Gaps','Complete','Complete and reviewed by a peer'),('Safety and ethics','Overlooked','Followed','Followed and taught to others')]
def C(slug,title,summary,outs,task,cond,standard,who,req,mods,extra,rub,ladder,jobs,level='L5 Specialist'):
    return dict(slug=slug,title=title,level=level,summary=summary,outs=outs,task=task,cond=cond,standard=standard,who=who,req=req,mods=mods,extra=extra,rubric=rub,ladder=ladder,jobs=jobs)
COURSES = [
C('biotechnology-and-life-sciences-innovation','Biotechnology and Life Sciences Innovation','Move a life-science idea from lab result to a tested, lawful and fundable product: validation, quality, intellectual property, regulation and a small-venture plan.',
 [('Define','a problem a life-science product can solve and who pays for it.'),('Apply','validation steps and quality records.'),('Analyse','trial data with simple statistics.'),('Evaluate','regulatory, ethical and biosafety risk.'),('Create','a venture plan and a pitch.')],
 'Take one lab-scale idea to a validation report, a protection plan and a venture plan.','About 12 weeks part-time. Access to lab data or a virtual lab, a mentor from industry or research, a team of two to four.','Claims are backed by repeated data, risks are listed with controls, ethics approval steps are named, and the plan shows costs and milestones.','Biotechnology graduates, research associates, founders, agri-biotech staff.','Biotechnology Foundations or equivalent.',
 [M('From problem to opportunity','Define',5,['Start from a need in health, farming, food or environment, not from a technique.','Size the need: how many people, how often, what they pay today.','Write a one-sentence problem and a one-sentence solution.','Check what already exists in papers and public records.'],'Need: post-harvest rot hitting banana growers. Idea: a natural coating from plant extract. Market check: three growers each lose about a fifth of the crop.','Write a problem sheet with numbers and sources.','Problem is specific, sized and sourced; solution is one sentence.','Why start from a need?','Products succeed when they solve a real problem.'),
  M('Validation: repeat and control','Apply',6,['Set a hypothesis and a pass limit before the test.','Use controls and at least three repeats.','Record conditions: temperature, batch, date, operator.','Report the spread, not only the average.'],'Treated bananas keep firm for 9 days against 5 days for controls, over 3 batches; the spread is one day.','Design and run a validation with three repeats.','Hypothesis, controls, repeats and limits are written first; results meet or miss the limit honestly.','Why set the pass limit first?','To avoid choosing the limit to fit the result.'),
  M('Data and statistics for decisions','Analyse',5,['Mean, spread and a simple comparison of two groups.','Charts that show every point.','What a small sample can and cannot show.','Keep raw data and the steps that produced each chart.'],'With 3 repeats, the gap of 4 days is larger than the spread of 1 day, so the effect is likely real but needs more repeats.','Analyse a data set and write a short finding.','Numbers are right; limits of the sample are stated.','What can a small sample not show?','That the effect is certain or applies everywhere.'),
  M('Quality and traceability','Apply',5,['Standard operating procedures: who, what, how, when.','Batch records and sample labels.','Calibration of balances, pipettes and meters.','Change control: write down any change and why.'],'A batch record lists lot numbers of extract, date, operator, volume, pH and result.','Write one procedure and one batch record.','Another person can repeat the work from your procedure.','What is a batch record for?','It lets anyone trace and repeat a batch.'),
  M('Intellectual property and data','Evaluate',4,['Patent, trademark, copyright and trade secret: what each protects.','Prior art search before you file.','Share data and materials under written terms.','Keep dated lab notebooks signed by a witness.'],'A coating recipe is kept as a trade secret while a patent search is done.','Write a protection plan for your idea.','Plan names the right tool for each asset and the next dated step.','What is prior art?','Earlier public knowledge that can block a patent.'),
  M('Biosafety, ethics and regulation','Evaluate',6,['Risk groups and containment levels.','Consent for human samples and ethics review for animals.','Approvals for food, drug, agri and device products follow different rules.','Local authority and national guidelines come first.'],'A food-contact coating needs a food-safety review before any sale.','Map the approvals your product needs.','Map names each authority, step and document.','Who decides approval for your product?','The authority for its product type, such as food, drug or agri.'),
  M('Scale-up and cost','Analyse',5,['Lab, pilot and production scale differ.','Cost of goods: materials, labour, utilities, loss.','Find the step that fails first at scale.','Use partners for pilot runs.'],'A pilot at 20 litres raises cost per litre by 30% because of cooling.','Cost one product at lab and pilot scale.','Costs add up and the first scale risk is named.','What is cost of goods?','Direct cost to make one unit.'),
  M('Venture plan and pitch','Create',5,['Customer, product, proof, money, team.','Milestones with dates and funds needed.','Grants, incubators and customers as funding sources.','Pitch in five minutes with one slide on proof.'],'A plan asking for a modest grant to run a field trial on 10 farms.','Write the plan and pitch it.','Plan has milestones, costs and proof; pitch fits five minutes.','What must the proof slide show?','The validated data and its limits.')],
 [('Why keep raw data?','So results can be checked.'),('Why name a witness on notebooks?','It dates and supports your records.')],
 RUB('Validation','Repeated with controls','Compliance','Approvals mapped and tracked'),
 LAD('Know basic biology words.','Explain how products are tested.','Help run lab work.','Validate an idea alone.','Take a product to pilot and plan its protection.','Lead a research and development team.','Set innovation and quality strategy for an institute.'),
 ['Research and development associate','Bioprocess scientist','Quality analyst','Technology transfer assistant','Biotechnology founder']),

C('textiles-and-fashion-sustainability','Textiles and Fashion Sustainability','Measure and cut the water, energy, chemical and waste footprint of fabric and garments, and build circular, fair-work fashion products.',
 [('Define','impact categories along the fashion chain.'),('Apply','measurement and reduction steps.'),('Analyse','a product life cycle.'),('Evaluate','claims, labels and suppliers.'),('Create','a circular product plan.')],
 'Measure the footprint of one product, set reduction targets and design a circular version with a costed plan.','About 12 weeks part-time. A product sample, supplier data or a unit visit, a mentor.','Measurements have units and sources, targets are dated, and every green claim is supported by evidence.','Designers, merchandisers, unit supervisors, artisan co-operative leaders.','Textiles and Sustainable Manufacturing or equivalent.',
 [M('Where the impact sits','Define',4,['Fibre growing, spinning, dyeing, making, transport, use, disposal.','Water, energy, chemicals, waste and working conditions.','The biggest impact is often in dyeing and in use.','Draw a map of one product chain.'],'A cotton shirt: most water in growing, most chemicals in dyeing, most energy in washing and drying over its life.','Map one product chain with the main impacts.','Map shows every step and one impact each.','Where is the water impact largest for cotton?','Growing the fibre.'),
  M('Measure what you use','Apply',6,['Litres of water, units of power, kilograms of chemical and waste per kilogram of fabric.','Meter and weigh; do not guess.','Daily log and monthly summary.','Compare with a simple target.'],'A dye house uses 120 litres per kilogram; the target is 90.','Measure one process for a week.','Log has units, dates and a summary.','Why measure per kilogram?','It lets you compare days and batches fairly.'),
  M('Cut water, energy and chemicals','Apply',6,['Reuse rinse water; fix leaks.','Heat recovery and efficient motors.','Choose safer dyes and fixing agents.','Treat effluent before release.'],'Counter-current rinsing cuts water use by about a third in one trial.','Write a reduction plan with three actions.','Each action has a saving, cost and owner.','Name two ways to cut water use.','Reuse rinse water and fix leaks.'),
  M('Waste, offcuts and circular design','Create',6,['Cut patterns to reduce offcuts.','Reuse offcuts in small products.','Design for repair and for recycling: single fibres, simple trims.','Take-back and resale.'],'Offcuts from kurtas are turned into bags and patchwork covers.','Design one circular product from waste.','Design shows material source, steps and end-of-life plan.','What does design for recycling mean?','Making items that can be taken apart and reprocessed.'),
  M('Fair work and artisan livelihoods','Evaluate',4,['Fair pay, hours and safe rooms.','Home workers and women in the chain.','Supplier code and visits.','Record grievances and fix them.'],'A code of conduct is signed by suppliers and checked on a visit.','Write a supplier code and a visit checklist.','Code covers pay, hours, safety and complaints.','Why visit suppliers?','To check the code is followed.'),
  M('Claims, labels and standards','Evaluate',4,['Avoid vague words such as eco-friendly without proof.','Use recognised labels only if certified.','Keep test reports and records.','Say what is true: percent recycled, litres saved.'],'Say 40% recycled cotton, with the test report on file.','Audit five claims.','Each claim is proved or rewritten.','Why avoid vague green words?','They can mislead and break rules.'),
  M('Costs, prices and markets','Analyse',5,['Cost of materials, labour and change.','Price for fair pay and margin.','Markets for sustainable products: online, craft fairs, institutions.','Tell the story with facts.'],'A 12% price premium is accepted by buyers who see the saving data.','Cost and price one product.','Numbers add up; premium is justified with facts.','How justify a price premium?','With true, verified benefits.'),
  M('Capstone: circular product plan','Create',5,['Choose one product.','Measure, target, redesign.','Cost and claim.','Present.'],'A plan to cut water by 25% and reuse 60% of offcuts within a year.','Present.','Plan has measures, targets, costs and proved claims.','What proves a green claim?','Test data and records.')],
 [('Why record test reports?','To prove claims.'),('Why design for repair?','It keeps products in use longer.')],
 RUB('Measurement','Units and sources','Claims','All proved'),
 LAD('Know chain steps.','Explain impacts.','Help measure.','Run a reduction plan alone.','Lead circular product lines.','Lead sustainability for a brand.','Set sector standards.'),
 ['Sustainability coordinator','Ethical production specialist','Sustainable fashion entrepreneur','Merchandiser','Compliance assistant']),

C('advanced-waste-management','Advanced Waste Management for Industry','Run industrial and hazardous waste systems: audits, treatment, recovery, extended producer duties, legal records and cost-saving circular projects.',
 [('Define','industrial waste classes and duties.'),('Apply','audits and storage rules.'),('Analyse','waste streams and costs.'),('Evaluate','treatment and recovery options.'),('Create','a compliance and reduction plan.')],
 'Audit a site, classify its streams and write a compliance and waste-reduction plan with costs and dates.','About 12 weeks part-time. A factory or training site, weighing scales, a mentor with site experience.','Streams are classified and weighed, records match the law, and the plan shows savings and owners.','Environment, health and safety staff, plant supervisors, recycling entrepreneurs.','Waste Management and Circular Resources or equivalent.',
 [M('Waste classes and duties','Define',4,['Hazardous, non-hazardous, e-waste, battery, plastic, biomedical and construction waste.','Duties of the maker of waste from source to disposal.','Producer duties for packaging and electronics.','Licences and authorised handlers.'],'Spent solvent is hazardous and may leave site only with an authorised handler and a manifest.','Classify ten streams from a site.','Each stream has a class, rule and handler.','Who may carry hazardous waste?','An authorised transporter with the manifest.'),
  M('Waste audit','Apply',6,['Walk the process and list every stream.','Weigh by stream for two weeks.','Find sources: spoilage, offcuts, packaging, spills.','Draw a flow of material in and waste out.'],'A plant finds 40% of its waste is packaging from one supplier.','Run an audit and draw the flow.','Weights, sources and flow are recorded.','What does a waste audit find?','What waste is made, where and how much.'),
  M('Storage, labelling and handling','Apply',5,['Separate incompatible wastes.','Labels with name, hazard, date.','Secondary containment for liquids.','Training and spill kits.'],'Acids and bases stored apart in bunded bays with labels and spill kits.','Inspect a store with a checklist.','Checklist finds and closes gaps.','Why keep incompatible wastes apart?','They can react and cause harm.'),
  M('Treatment and recovery options','Evaluate',6,['Reduce, reuse, recycle, recover energy, treat, dispose.','Solvent recovery, metal recovery, co-processing and secure landfill.','Cost per tonne and carbon of each route.','Check that the partner is authorised.'],'Solvent recovery cuts disposal cost by more than half and lowers purchase of fresh solvent.','Compare three routes for one stream.','Table has cost, risk and legal check.','Which comes first, recycle or reduce?','Reduce.'),
  M('Records, reporting and audits','Apply',5,['Manifests, registers and annual returns.','Keep copies for the stated years.','Prepare for inspection.','Fix findings within dates.'],'An annual return lists type, quantity and handler for each stream.','Build a register and a return.','Entries are complete and agree with weights.','Why keep manifests?','Proof of lawful transfer.'),
  M('Data, sensors and improvement','Analyse',5,['Track waste per unit of product.','Simple sensors and weighbridge data.','Charts by week and by shift.','Set targets and review.'],'Waste per tonne of product falls from 42 kg to 31 kg after a change.','Chart four weeks of data.','Chart shows trend and one action.','What is waste per unit of product?','Waste divided by output.'),
  M('Industrial symbiosis and producer duties','Evaluate',4,['Waste of one firm as input to another.','Take-back and packaging plans.','Contracts with clear quality limits.','Share savings fairly.'],'Fly ash from a plant goes to a brick maker under a contract.','Find two exchange options.','Options have buyers, quality limits and savings.','What is industrial symbiosis?','One firm waste becomes another firm input.'),
  M('Capstone: compliance and reduction plan','Create',5,['Audit.','Classify.','Plan with costs.','Present to a mentor.'],'A plan that cuts disposal cost by 20% in a year.','Present.','Plan is lawful, costed and dated.','What proves the plan works?','Lower waste per unit and clean records.')],
 [('Why weigh waste?','Measure change.'),('Why check partners are authorised?','The maker of waste stays responsible.')],
 RUB('Audit','Weights and flow','Compliance','Records inspection-ready'),
 LAD('Know waste classes.','Explain duties.','Help with audits.','Run site compliance alone.','Design reduction and recovery projects.','Lead environment, health and safety.','Set industrial waste policy.'),
 ['Environment, health and safety officer','Waste management supervisor','Recycling entrepreneur','Compliance officer','Circular supply chain analyst']),
]
